id: pm-github-d26g
title: Use the pm SDK for GitHub import lifecycle persistence
description: "Replace the audited manual item lock and document/history write boundary in import-fidelity.ts with mutateItem, retaining source lifetimes, idempotency and hooks. Assess commitItemMutations for ordinary conditional fields. Related SDK adoption: pm-github-gh83; lifecycle behavior: pm-github-c093. Closeout history already uses the SDK and its remaining provider attribution rules stay intact."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[2]: refactor,sdk-adoption
created_at: "2026-10-25T15:32:07.865Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-26T03:15:55.541Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-26T03:15:48.066Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-25T18:19:28.000Z"
author: codex-agent
resolution: "Delivered by PR #180, merge fcd9f93e28e85b170506ceac507d82a911173683, merged 2026-10-25T18:19:28Z. import-fidelity.ts persistImportFidelity uses mutateItem for the lock/document/history boundary and lazily derives hook fields from the actual SDK mutation. test/sdk-adoption.test.ts exercises guards, strict ownership, hooks/no-op retries and clock-boundary patch parity. docs/sdk-adoption-1025.md records ordinary conditional-field assessment and retained provider attribution rules."
expected_result: "SDK lifecycle persistence preserves source lifetime metadata, idempotency and exact import hooks under native governance."
actual_result: "Four focused SDK regressions pass on main; inspected mutateItem callback and lazy hook projection satisfy scoped adoption, with documented native refusal/storage differences."
