comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-25T15:32:18.083Z",codex-agent,"Audit assessment: import-fidelity.ts manually owns the fenced item/history boundary; replace it with mutateItem using skipNoop and exact source timestamp edits in the mutation callback. Existing ordinary conditional fields already pass through commitItemMutations in index.ts; finalization also owns reserved native lifecycle timestamps so splitting it into a second bulk field transaction would break its single boundary. closeout.ts already uses readHistoryEntries/getHistoryPath/verifyHistoryEntries; chronology and attribution remain provider domain logic as directed by the audit. Validate with real tracker copies without git, immutable origin/main build comparison, hook payloads, policy refusals, rollback and retry tests."
  "2026-10-25T15:37:28.424Z",codex-agent,"Replacement complete: mutateItem now owns lifecycle locking, item/history persistence, append rollback, derived-index maintenance and hooks. Source timestamps, link-only owner preservation, normalization, chronology checks and no-op detection remain in the callback. SDK createHistoryEntry is used only for the existing JSON-pointer hook projection. No SDK API blocker remains. Differential proof on built origin/main 1cb49ac06bfee8d1193137367f86a36798a1040e and two complete public tracker snapshots passed 14/14 scenarios without git; normal cases have identical item/history bytes and import hook payloads, with byte-stable no-op retries. Intentional differences: transactional guard and strict ownership refusal, SDK missing-item diagnostic, additional runtime index lock observations. SDK native storage migration and governance contracts are documented in docs/sdk-adoption-1025.md."
  "2026-10-25T15:37:29.479Z",codex-agent,"Per-replacement revert proof: restored only persistImportFidelity and its imports from origin/main, ran node --test test/sdk-adoption.test.ts: exit 1, 1 pass / 2 fail / 0 skipped. The beforeMutation guard and strict-ownership cases both failed with missing expected rejection; hook/retry compatibility passed. Restored the SDK implementation: same command passes 3/3, 0 skipped. npm run typecheck, npm run lint and npm run build:test also pass. The production before/after replay is test/sdk-adoption-differential.ts; complete snapshot digests stayed unchanged."
  "2026-10-25T16:05:09.250Z",codex-agent,"PR opened ready for review: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/180. CI source head cd75897ec50399a996be8680b7830bd5836f4004: both bun-release jobs (Node 22 and 26) passed; completed Node 22 gate reports 1498/1498 tests, 0 failures/skips, exact 100/100/100/100 across 19 authored modules. The Node 26 npm release step also passed and its native Bun acceptance step is running. CI run: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/40208204021. Local native Bun targeted regressions passed 3/3. Full local npm identity reproduction and remaining CI jobs are still running. Independent review remains missing: Greptile reports its trial ended; skipped/neutral automated checks are not approval."
  "2026-10-25T16:15:54.374Z",codex-agent,"Expanded the differential proof to assert diagnostic exit codes as well as messages and structured refusal codes. All 14/14 scenarios pass again. Intentional SDK classifications: missing item changes generic exit 1 to not-found exit 3; transactional guard and strict-ownership refusals use conflict exit 4. README and docs/sdk-adoption-1025.md document these values. Normal item/history bytes and import hook payloads still match the built origin/main baseline exactly, with byte-stable retries and unchanged public source snapshots."
  "2026-10-25T16:29:46.604Z",codex-agent,"Implementation and local verification complete. Full local npm run release:check under an isolated home and Git identity passed: 1498/1498 tests, zero failures/cancellations/skips, exact 100/100/100/100 across 19 authored modules, zero production vulnerabilities; privacy, docstring, lint, duplication, pack, changelog and attestation passed. CI source cd75897ec50399a996be8680b7830bd5836f4004 has all four npm/Bun release-gate steps green on Node 22/26; three jobs complete and only Node 22 native Bun acceptance is still running. The final evidence commit includes explicit diagnostic exit-code assertions and documentation; differential replay remains 14/14. Final head status and counts will be published in PR 180 and its checks: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/180/checks. Releasing the implementation claim and leaving the item in progress for orchestrator verification; no SDK API blocker, merge or release. Independent review remains pending."
  "2026-10-25T17:08:39.996Z",codex-agent,"Final review reproduced an exact-hook edge case in the initial SDK adapter: if the clock advances between its mutation callback and SDK persistence, eager changed-field projection can omit updated_at while the actual appended patch includes it. A real SDK/temp-tracker reproduction fails on the initial adapter. Reclaiming implementation work to derive the JSON-pointer projection lazily from the SDK-owned document after clock/format enrichment; this also removes the redundant local mutation clock. Add a deterministic clock-boundary regression, repeat differential/revert proof and final-head gates. No SDK mock or upstream API blocker is needed."
  "2026-10-25T17:14:21.542Z",codex-agent,"Clock-boundary correction verified: lazy SDK patch projection removes the local native timestamp assignment and JSON no-op comparison. SDK skipNoop and the final SDK-enriched document now supply both exact hook fields and no-op behavior. node --test test/sdk-adoption.test.ts and bun test --timeout 600000 test/sdk-adoption.test.ts each pass 4/4, zero skipped. Behavioral revert to the initial eager SDK adapter: 3 passed / 1 failed, missing updated_at in hook fields. Revert only persistImportFidelity and imports to origin/main: 2 passed / 2 failed (transactional guard and ownership); both compatibility cases pass. Restoring the corrected SDK function passes 4/4. Rebuilt production differential replay passes 14/14 with unchanged public snapshots and documented SDK exit codes. Superseded candidate CI was canceled after reproducing the clock defect; it is not final evidence. Fresh final-head npm/Bun gates are required."
  "2026-10-25T17:15:55.971Z",codex-agent,"Corrected implementation is ready for final-head verification. Local typecheck, build:test, lint, docstring and duplication all passed after the clock correction. The linked pm test run passes all four regressions. Differential proof is 14/14; original-function revert is 2 pass / 2 fail and eager-projection revert is 3 pass / 1 fail. Production diff from origin/main is 34 removed / 27 added lines (24 removed / 17 added ignoring indentation), net seven fewer lines. The SDK now owns the native clock and skipNoop completely; createHistoryEntry supplies only a lazy exact hook projection. No SDK API blocker. Releasing the claim while the final CI matrix verifies the new commit; the authoritative final result is PR 180 and https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/180/checks. Leave this item in progress for orchestrator verification; do not merge or release."
  "2026-10-26T03:14:57.228Z",codex-agent,"Closure audit on main fcd9f93e28e85b170506ceac507d82a911173683: merged PR #180 (fcd9f93e28e85b170506ceac507d82a911173683, merged 2026-10-25T18:19:28Z). import-fidelity.ts persistImportFidelity uses mutateItem for the lock/document/history boundary and lazily derives hook fields from the actual SDK mutation. test/sdk-adoption.test.ts exercises guards, strict ownership, hooks/no-op retries and clock-boundary patch parity. docs/sdk-adoption-1025.md records ordinary conditional-field assessment and retained provider attribution rules. All scoped acceptance criteria are represented by the inspected implementation and regressions. Existing behavioural revert evidence is retained; this tracker-only audit changes no runtime functions."
